            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-saving-your-work-with-git\">4. Saving your work with git</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">git records snapshots of your files. You'll use four commands all semester:</span>\n<div class=\"language-sh codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>git<span class=\"w\"> </span>clone<span class=\"w\"> </span>&lt;url&gt;<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\"># copy an assignment repo to your computer</span>\ngit<span class=\"w\"> </span>add<span class=\"w\"> </span>hw01.py<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\"># choose what goes into the snapshot</span>\ngit<span class=\"w\"> </span>commit<span class=\"w\"> </span>-m<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Finish task 1\"</span>\ngit<span class=\"w\"> </span>push<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"c1\"># upload it; this is how you submit</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"5-when-things-go-wrong\">5. When things go wrong</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Errors are normal. Python tells you <strong>where</strong> the error happened and <strong>what kind</strong> it is. Read the <em>last line</em> first.</span></span>"
          }
        }
